Runs 100 G38.2 probes in AUTO mode and fails on "Queue is not empty
after probing" (#3650).

After a probe, read-ahead waits for the EMC_TASK_PLAN_SYNCH that follows
it, then reads the next line, whose read_inputs() wants an empty motion
queue.  Motion acknowledges the probe command in motion-command-handler
but only updates the queue depth and in-position flag in
motion-controller.  A status snapshot taken in between still shows motion
idle, so the SYNCH completes at once, and if the next snapshot shows the
probe in the queue, read_inputs() fails.

That gap is normally a few microseconds wide.  probe.hal puts servo_delay
between the two functions, a busy wait that varies on each servo period,
so about half of the probes see it.  Task must not clear the read-ahead
wait while the queue it is about to check is not empty.
